  "unreadable": [
    "power-header position 1: top hole of the power header has no label (unlabeled pad)"
  ],
  "notes": "Labels use GPIO names from the diagram callouts; board silkscreen spellings (3v3, Rst, Gnd, Vin, 24, 13, TX...) put first in functions where they differ, followed by the CircuitPython name. Image note: the TX and RX pins may be connected to D0 or D1 depending on the direction of the switch next to the Boot button and the TX pin. MicroSD slot signals (SD_CD, SCK, MOSI, MISO, SDIO_DATA1/2, SD_CS), NEOPIXEL and the unlabeled 2x5 SWD header are skipped. The right digital side is drawn as two separate headers (gap between D8 and D7), transcribed as two connectors. ICSP header mapping follows the leader lines and silkscreen (Rst/SCK/MISO top row, Gnd/MOSI/5V bottom row)."
}